Based on the excerpts provided, the **Malicious Damage, Intentional Damage or damage by vandals** insured event states that RAA will cover "loss or damage to the Insured Property" caused by Malicious Damage, Intentional Damage, or vandalism [RAA Contents PDS, page 47]. The excerpts do not single out fences as excluded from this particular insured event.

However, this cover does **not** apply in the following circumstances [RAA Contents PDS, page 47]:
- chips, scratches, dents or any superficial markings to the Insured Property;
- wear and tear, or damage caused over a period of time;
- loss or damage caused by you, your Guest, an Occupier or any Co-Insured;
- loss or damage caused by a person who entered your Home with the consent (implied or otherwise) of you, your Guest, an Occupier or any Co-Insured; or
- loss or damage that has not been reported to the police.

Separately, the excerpts show that **wind damage** to gates or fences is excluded if the fence "was not structurally sound or was not maintained in a reasonable manner prior to the loss or damage occurring" [RAA Contents PDS, page 45] — but this exclusion appears under a different insured event (relating to storm/wind), not the Malicious Damage event.

I do not have an excerpt that explicitly confirms whether fences are included within, or excluded from, the definition of "Insured Property" for the Malicious Damage insured event spec
